.TH XUR.STD.HASH 7 "2026-11-19" "xur 0.1.3" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.hash \- cryptographic and non-cryptographic hashes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
use std::hash;

let digest = hash::sha256(data);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::hash
provides common hash functions. All functions accept a
.B bytes
argument (a byte list or byte literal).
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B crc32(data: bytes) -> int
CRC-32 checksum as an integer.
.TP
.B sha256(data: bytes) -> str
SHA-256 digest as a lowercase hex string.
.TP
.B sha256_bytes(data: bytes) -> bytes
SHA-256 digest as raw bytes (32 bytes).
.TP
.B md5(data: bytes) -> str
MD5 digest as a lowercase hex string.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::hash;
use std::io;

fn main() {
    let data = "hello".bytes();
    io::println("sha256: {}", hash::sha256(data));
    io::println("md5:    {}", hash::md5(data));
    io::println("crc32:  {}", hash::crc32(data));
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std (7),
.BR xur.std.bytes (7)
